<title>FRANCE: French Gaullist deputy opposes Socialist audit.</title>
<headline>French Gaullist deputy opposes Socialist audit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A conservative parliamentarian charged on Wednesday that Socialist Prime Minister Lionel Jospin's plan to conduct an audit of France's public finances threatened the shift to a single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;I fear that by playing on the excessive public deficits, the Socialist government is looking for an excuse to put off the adoption of the euro,&quot; Gaullst RPR Deputy Patrick Devedjian said in a radio interview.</p>
<p>Jospin's government took office after sweeping the previous centre-right government from power in a June 1 parliamentary</p>
